message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Statistical Horizon: A Scaling Benchmark and Procedural Caution for Institutional Use of AI Text Watermarking"
authors:
  - family-names: "Van Ryn"
    given-names: "Henri F."
    email: "henri.vanryn@gmail.com"
version: "5.8"
date-released: "2026-06-23"
type: article
keywords:
  - "AI watermarking"
  - "statistical inference"
  - "forensic science"
  - "institutional reliance"
  - "machine learning governance"
  - "digital provenance"
  - "AI policy"
abstract: >-
  AI text watermarking has evolved from academic speculation into industrial
  practice. This paper formalizes the Statistical Horizon as a structural scaling
  benchmark for finite-sample watermark detectability and argues that watermark
  detections should be treated as probabilistic, assumption-sensitive forensic
  signals rather than proof of authorship.
